# Offline build material handoff

Checked locally on 2026-10-13; no VM, container, SSH, ADB, or device command was run. Exact paths/hashes and disk statistics are in `build-environment.json`.

The retained Colima profile is `e5-openwrt-prep`, configured for aarch64 VZ, 12 CPUs, 24 GiB memory, a 110 GiB data disk and 24 GiB root disk. Its host-agent log records VZ stopped at 22:08. Host available space at this check was 196,359,770,112 bytes (about 183 GiB). The sparse disk files occupy approximately 24.21 GB plus 3.63 GB on the host; their logical lengths are not guest filesystem free-space measurements. Guest free space and cached container health remain unverified because this task did not enter the VM.

The original host build directory is `/REDACTED_HOST_PATH`. The recorded guest source path is `/mnt/lima-colima-e5-openwrt-prep/e5-build/source`. The source main commit is `569f13d4ce15585f70817c2a1e03bb574a84720b`, kernel commit `020b970e351eee3887e6caaf2d653926e7086e44`, and the built kernel release is `6.18.54-e5-mobile4-g020b970e351e-dirty`. The host source has the intentionally retained `boot/init` adaptation; do not reset it or silently remove the diagnostic write cap. Frozen `kernel-adaptations.patch` and `local-source-adaptations.patch` preserve the earlier implementation provenance.

Existing method references are `vm-build-kernel.sh` (Docker `e5-mainline-build`, object cache volume `e5-feature-kernel-objects`), `vm-build-packages.sh`, `vm-build-block.sh`, and `vm-build-bundle.sh`. The bundle wrapper sets OpenWrt 25.12.5, 2 GiB image, features enabled, Docker feature disabled, mainline kernel path, this device's stock B and misc-header inputs, static BusyBox, and fixed build epoch; it invokes `openwrt/make-flash-bundle.sh`. That builder regenerates the rootfs with matching kernel modules in mainline mode. Kernel recompilation is not inherently required for a userland-only WAN script candidate. A new complete image would still need its new source/patch hashes, content/runtime audit, own-device provenance and restricted deployment/recovery review.

Do not rerun the old wrappers verbatim for a new candidate: their hard-coded `HOST_BUILD` copies outputs over the original `release`, `bundle`, `kernel`, logs and marker files. Instead, retain the originals, create a separately named source/output tree, review the minimal patch there, copy/adapt the wrapper's input and output paths, and write a new manifest. The Colima configuration currently mounts only the original host build directory; a separate host destination needs an explicitly reviewed mount or an isolated new output subdirectory that does not overwrite frozen files. `vm-prepare.sh` performs package updates and git fetching, so it is not needed just to inspect or reuse an already prepared cache.

The existing generic release and the device's retained runtime image serve different purposes. The pre-D0 runtime snapshot includes this device's evolved private NV copies and settings; D0 may have changed those files again. Do not use a fresh generic rootfs as a transparent replacement for that runtime. Tomorrow's read-only snapshot, a narrow migration/patch plan, and recoverable ordinary-file transaction must precede any future rootfs update. This handoff provides paths and method references, not authorization or a runnable flashing script.
